	<h2>To the Theatre</h2>
	<p class="lead l pc">“I want to see the instant costume change!” “Do men really play female roles?” If you’re wondering, then head to the theatre and watch an actual production! This is a guide to help you appreciate Kabuki, whether it is your first time, your second time, or you want to enjoy a variety of productions.</p>
</section>
<section id="content">
	<section id="left">
		<article>
			<h3><span>Where</span> do I watch?</h3>
			<div class="img_R no-border pc mt-10"><img src="images/ct8_index_1.jpg" width="150" height="101" alt="Where do I watch?"></div>
			<p class="lead pc">In cities like Tokyo, Osaka, and Kyoto there are theatres that regularly stage kabuki for a month at a time; there are also regional and irregular performances.</p>
			<ul>
				<li><a href="theatre1.html#a">Theatres and tickets<span class="b">National Theatre</span><span class="pclist">Production style / Performances for beginners<br>
					Membership associations / Buying tickets</span><span class="mlist">Production style</span><span class="mlist">Performances for beginners</span><span class="mlist">Membership associations</span><span class="mlist">Buying tickets</span><span class="b">Other theatres</span><span>Tokyo, Osaka, Kyoto, Nagoya</span></a></li>
				<li><a href="theatre1.html#b">Selecting seats</a></li>
			</ul>
		</article>
	</section>
	<section id="right">
		<article>
			<h3><span>How</span> do I watch?</h3>
			<div class="img_R no-border pc"><img src="images/ct8_index_2.png" width="187" height="130" alt="How do I watch?"></div>
			<p class="lead pc">There are no complicated rules such as a dress code when you watch Kabuki, but there are lots of ways to enjoy the performance even more if you know about them in advance.</p>
			<ul>
				<li><a href="theatre2.html#a">Before you go</a></li>
				<li><a href="theatre2.html#b">During the performance</a></li>
				<li><a href="theatre2.html#c">Viewing manners</a></li>
			</ul>
		</article>
	</section>
</section>
